1
00:00:00,500 --> 00:00:05,326
A tank can still have water when it is already time to arrange

2
00:00:05,326 --> 00:00:09,409
the next supply. Jal Rakshak helps one hostel caretaker see that

3
00:00:09,409 --> 00:00:11,636
decision before the tank runs empty.

4
00:00:12,500 --> 00:00:16,278
This is a working local prototype for one site.

5
00:00:16,278 --> 00:00:20,056
The dashboard connects the latest reading, reserve level, delivery

6
00:00:20,056 --> 00:00:22,995
lead time and a clear next action.

7
00:00:22,995 --> 00:00:25,513
Every demonstration reading is labeled simulated.

8
00:00:26,500 --> 00:00:29,694
The planning deadline comes before the reserve crossing.

9
00:00:29,694 --> 00:00:33,287
It subtracts supply lead time and an operating buffer.

10
00:00:33,287 --> 00:00:37,679
Reserve breach and empty tank time stay separate, so the caretaker

11
00:00:37,679 --> 00:00:40,473
can understand the reason for the recommendation.

12
00:00:42,500 --> 00:00:44,589
An observed workspace starts empty.

13
00:00:44,589 --> 00:00:47,096
Missing or stale readings stay unknown.

14
00:00:47,096 --> 00:00:51,691
The operator must declare a reading error bound and its basis.

15
00:00:51,691 --> 00:00:56,287
A small bound prompts review, and the interface explains that declaration

16
00:00:56,287 --> 00:00:57,540
is not calibration.

17
00:00:58,500 --> 00:01:01,557
What if the next supply arrives late?

18
00:01:01,557 --> 00:01:05,487
A preview compares that plan without changing the readings.

19
00:01:05,487 --> 00:01:08,980
Historical hourly demand informs the outlook, while unconfirmed

20
00:01:08,980 --> 00:01:12,473
delivery plans cannot extend the conservative planning deadline.

21
00:01:13,500 --> 00:01:17,654
In this generated scenario, sustained excess usage opens an incident.

22
00:01:17,654 --> 00:01:22,223
The app shows the abnormal depletion and the evidence behind it.

23
00:01:22,223 --> 00:01:27,623
It does not pretend to locate a leak or identify a physical fault.

24
00:01:29,500 --> 00:01:33,033
The caretaker reviews the exact notice and explicitly approves

25
00:01:33,033 --> 00:01:36,958
it. Approval belongs to this incident and this evidence revision.

26
00:01:36,958 --> 00:01:40,098
The receipt means the notice was saved locally.

27
00:01:40,098 --> 00:01:45,201
It does not mean a tanker was booked or a supplier was contacted.

28
00:01:46,500 --> 00:01:50,036
Recording a repair does not close the incident.

29
00:01:50,036 --> 00:01:54,015
Recovery needs three fresh independent normal readings after the

30
00:01:54,015 --> 00:01:56,225
intervention and adequate planning margin.

31
00:01:56,225 --> 00:01:58,877
The activity trail records what happened.

32
00:01:58,877 --> 00:02:03,740
New observations support the recovery decision; a button or a message

33
00:02:03,740 --> 00:02:05,508
cannot provide that evidence.

34
00:02:06,500 --> 00:02:10,287
The original synthetic holdout has no late reserve predictions.

35
00:02:10,287 --> 00:02:14,494
Stress cases still include twelve late predictions, and early warnings

36
00:02:14,494 --> 00:02:16,598
and false alerts remain concerns.

37
00:02:16,598 --> 00:02:21,226
Tests prove local behavior; they do not prove accuracy on real

38
00:02:21,226 --> 00:02:21,647
tanks.

39
00:02:22,500 --> 00:02:28,400
The repository includes Lambda, a SAM template, and a boto three

40
00:02:28,400 --> 00:02:31,618
Dynamo DB adapter. GitHub checks pass.

41
00:02:31,618 --> 00:02:36,982
Live AWS execution remains unverified; this demo uses local SQLite

42
00:02:36,982 --> 00:02:37,519
storage.

43
00:02:38,500 --> 00:02:42,148
Jal Rakshak connects reserve planning, explicit approval and reading

44
00:02:42,148 --> 00:02:44,580
supported recovery in one caretaker workflow.

45
00:02:44,580 --> 00:02:49,039
The next milestone is a real tank log and caretaker feedback.

46
00:02:49,039 --> 00:02:53,497
Explore the public source, run the demo and inspect the evidence.
